 ## Overview
-Grendel-GS is a distributed optimization framework for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that partitions the Gaussian primitive list across multiple GPUs to overcome single-device memory limits [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [TideGS](7350-tidegs.md), which streams data from disk on a single machine, Grendel-GS distributes the parameter table across a GPU cluster, enabling training on scenes with billions of primitives by leveraging inter-GPU communication [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the differentiable rasterization core defined in [Optimization and Training Efficiency](9264-optimization-and-training-efficiency.md) but modifies the data flow to support multi-GPU parallelism.
